    'For any nextAction with risk "write" or "external", fill in "detail" with one plain line naming exactly what it will do and why (the target + the gist), and name that same action + reason in report.summary — so I always know what I am approving.',
    'If this step produced actual code changes, you MUST ALSO include "diff" inside report — the verbatim, unedited output of `git --no-pager diff` — so I can review the prepared change as a preview. If it produced a message/email/newsletter to send, ALSO include "draft" inside report with the ready-to-use body text. Do NOT commit or push and do NOT send anything unless I explicitly asked — prepare it and report the diff/draft instead. To actually SEND an email or post a message, do NOT call internal endpoints like /api/share/email or /api/share/teams (they only make a local .eml draft and bypass approval) and do NOT send it yourself — instead offer a nextAction with "risk":"external" (e.g. "Send email"), which is executed for real with WorkIQ (do_action /me/sendMail) once I approve.',
